# Integrate Sunmi V2 Thermal Printer for Mobile Receipts

This plan outlines the steps to connect our web-based React POS to the Sunmi V2's internal thermal printer, formatting the output to look like a professional 58mm mobile receipt.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Architectural Decision: How we connect to the printer**
> Since web browsers (like Chrome) cannot directly talk to internal hardware printers, we need a bridge. 
> 
> **Proposed Approach (Recommended): Capacitor JS**
> We will use **Capacitor** (by Ionic) to wrap our React frontend into a native Android `.apk`. Capacitor allows us to write standard React code while using "Plugins" to talk to native Android hardware (like the Sunmi Printer SDK). This gives the POS a true "Mobile App" feel without rewriting it in Java or Kotlin.

