## Proposed Changes

We will implement this in three main phases entirely within the `pos-frontend` directory.

### Phase 1: Capacitor Integration (Making it a Mobile App)
- Initialize Capacitor in the `pos-frontend` project (`npm install @capacitor/core @capacitor/cli`).
- Add the Android platform (`npx cap add android`).
- This will allow us to build an `app-release.apk` that can be installed directly onto the Sunmi V2 device.

### Phase 2: Sunmi Printer SDK Plugin
- Install a Capacitor Sunmi Printer plugin (e.g., `capacitor-sunmi-printer` or similar open-source bridge).
- This plugin connects JavaScript commands directly to the `SunmiPrinterService` built into the device.

### Phase 3: Receipt Formatting Service
#### [NEW] `pos-frontend/src/services/printerService.ts`
We will create a service that takes a `Transaction` object and translates it into Sunmi thermal printer commands. It will handle the 58mm layout:

```typescript
export const printReceipt = async (transaction, cartItems) => {
  // 1. Header (Centered, Bold)
  await SunmiPrinter.setAlignment('CENTER');
  await SunmiPrinter.setFontSize(24);
  await SunmiPrinter.printText("MY STORE NAME\n");
  
  // 2. Transaction Details (Left Aligned)
  await SunmiPrinter.setAlignment('LEFT');
  await SunmiPrinter.setFontSize(16);
  await SunmiPrinter.printText(`Date: ${transaction.date}\n`);
  await SunmiPrinter.printText(`Receipt #: ${transaction.id}\n`);
  await SunmiPrinter.printText("--------------------------------\n");
  
  // 3. Items (Left/Right justified mapping)
  cartItems.forEach(item => {
    // Format: "1x Coffee           P150.00"
    await SunmiPrinter.printColumnsText(
      [`${item.qty}x ${item.name}`, `P${item.total}`],
      [20, 12], // Column widths for 58mm paper
      [0, 2]    // 0=Left align, 2=Right align
    );
  });
  
  await SunmiPrinter.printText("--------------------------------\n");
  
  // 4. Total (Large Font, Right Aligned)
  await SunmiPrinter.setAlignment('RIGHT');
  await SunmiPrinter.setFontSize(30);
  await SunmiPrinter.printText(`TOTAL: P${transaction.total}\n`);
  
  // 5. Footer & Cut
  await SunmiPrinter.setAlignment('CENTER');
  await SunmiPrinter.printQRCode("https://mystore.com", 6, 3);
  await SunmiPrinter.printText("\nThank you for shopping!\n\n\n");
  
  // Cut the paper (if supported by the specific Sunmi model)
  await SunmiPrinter.cutPaper();
}
```

#### [MODIFY] `pos-frontend/src/components/CheckoutModal.tsx`
- Update the successful checkout flow. When a transaction successfully saves to the database, we will call `printReceipt(transaction, cart)` to automatically push the receipt to the Sunmi printer.

### Phase 4: Standard Web-to-Printer Fallback (CSS Print Media)
If the system is ever run on a standard PC Chrome browser connected to a USB thermal POS printer, we will implement a CSS `@media print` stylesheet to ensure the web print dialog produces the exact same 58mm layout as the mobile version.

#### [NEW] `pos-frontend/src/styles/ReceiptPrint.css`
```css
@media print {
  /* Hide the entire application UI */
  body * {
    visibility: hidden;
  }
  
  /* Only show the hidden receipt container */
  #printable-receipt, #printable-receipt * {
    visibility: visible;
  }
  
  /* Force a 58mm width layout and standard thermal fonts */
  #printable-receipt {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    width: 58mm; /* Standard Sunmi / Thermal paper width */
    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: #000;
  }

  .receipt-header { text-align: center; font-weight: bold; font-size: 16px; }
  .receipt-item-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
  .receipt-total { text-align: right; font-weight: bold; font-size: 18px; }
}
```

